<div class="mb-7 flex flex-col justify-between gap-5 sm:flex-row sm:items-end"><div><p class="mb-2 text-[11px] font-semibold uppercase tracking-[.18em] text-accent">Administration</p><h1 class="font-serif text-4xl font-medium tracking-tight sm:text-5xl">Role overview</h1><p class="mt-2 max-w-2xl text-sm leading-6 text-muted">AuthService currently defines two assignable admin-console roles. Permissions are enforced by API services and gateway policies.</p></div><a href="{{ route('admin.staff') }}" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-lg bg-ink px-4 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-accent"><span class="material-symbols-outlined text-base">group</span>Manage staff accounts</a></div>
<div class="mb-6 grid grid-cols-1 gap-4 lg:grid-cols-2"><article class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-5 shadow-card"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="material-symbols-outlined rounded-xl bg-amber-50 p-2 text-amber-800" aria-hidden="true">admin_panel_settings</span><div><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Admin</h2><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted">Global administrator role</p></div></div><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-muted">Required for gateway routes using the <code class="rounded bg-canvas px-1.5 py-0.5 text-xs">AdminOnly</code> policy and AuthService staff-management endpoints. Admin accounts can access protected operational areas such as orders, payments, delivery administration, reviews, promotions, and notifications.</p></article><article class="rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white p-5 shadow-card"><div class="flex items-start gap-3"><span class="material-symbols-outlined rounded-xl bg-soft p-2 text-accent" aria-hidden="true">badge</span><div><h2 class="text-lg font-semibold">Staff</h2><p class="mt-1 text-xs text-muted">Operational staff role</p></div></div><p class="mt-4 text-sm leading-6 text-muted">Allowed by selected service endpoints for catalog operations, standard inventory operations, and support ticket work. Staff is not accepted by AdminOnly routes.</p></article></div>
<section class="overflow-hidden rounded-2xl border border-line bg-white shadow-card" aria-labelledby="permission-overview"><div class="border-b border-line px-5 py-4"><h2 id="permission-overview" class="text-lg font-semibold">Endpoint authorization overview</h2><p class="mt-1 text-xs leading-5 text-muted">This reflects role checks found in gateway and service routes. It is not a configurable permission matrix.</p></div><div class="overflow-x-auto"><table class="min-w-[760px] w-full text-left text-sm"><caption class="sr-only">Feature access by the built-in Admin and Staff roles</caption><thead class="bg-canvas text-[11px] uppercase tracking-wide text-muted"><tr><th scope="col" class="px-5 py-3">Protected area</th><th scope="col" class="px-5 py-3">Admin</th><th scope="col" class="px-5 py-3">Staff</th><th scope="col" class="px-5 py-3">Authorization source</th></tr></thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-line"><tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium">Staff and role management</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-emerald-800">Allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-500">Not allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-xs text-muted">Gateway AdminOnly + AuthService Admin role</td></tr><tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium">Catalog create, update, and delete operations</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-emerald-800">Allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-emerald-800">Allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-xs text-muted">ProductService Staff, Admin</td></tr><tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium">Standard inventory operations</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-emerald-800">Allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-emerald-800">Allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-xs text-muted">InventoryService Admin, Staff checks</td></tr><tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium">Privileged inventory administration</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-emerald-800">Allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-500">Not allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-xs text-muted">InventoryService Admin role</td></tr><tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium">Support tickets and complaints</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-emerald-800">Allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-emerald-800">Allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-xs text-muted">SupportService Admin, Staff</td></tr><tr><td class="px-5 py-4 font-medium">Orders, payments, delivery, reviews, promotions, notifications, customer administration</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-emerald-800">Allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-500">Not allowed</td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-xs text-muted">Service Admin role checks</td></tr></tbody></table></div></section>
<aside class="mt-6 rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 p-5"><h2 class="text-sm font-semibold text-amber-950">Role and permission API limitations</h2><p class="mt-2 text-xs leading-5 text-amber-900">AuthService supports assigning only Admin or Staff. There is no custom role CRUD, granular permission catalog, or per-permission assignment API. The access overview is read-only and derived from current authorization attributes. Changes to staff roles are confirmed and enforced again by AuthService.</p></aside>
